HST Office: HST Công thức in Math: arc and text arrows, MathType 4-7 reader, templates.

New StarMath constructs: "widearc {AB}" (arc over a name, geometry) and the arrows with text
over and under them, "{over} xrightarrow {under}", xleftarrow, xrightleftarrows and
xrightleftharpoons (reaction conditions in chemistry); the arrow stretches with its texts.
They are written to and read from OMML and RTF. The OMML import also keeps a relation that
starts a line ("= 105") and a single left script, which were lost on a .docx round trip.

MathType::Parse hands MTEF version 5 ("Equation.DSMT4", MathType 4-7) to the HST reader
(starmath/source/hst/mtef5*, written clean-room from a behaviour spec) and applies the
equation's own base size. A failed conversion returns false, so callers keep the OLE object.

The Elements panel gets the Mẫu Toán, Mẫu Vật lí and Mẫu Hoá học template categories (and opens
on them for "Mẫu công thức"); the formula editor gets the "Mẫu công thức" template bar.
The logic lives in HST-owned files under starmath/source/hst/.

